# Godot 4+ specific ignores
.godot/
/android/
perf_log.csv
perf_log.csv.import
perf_log.*.translation

# Heavy binary assets (models, textures) -- not tracked in git, only the
# project files that reference them. See crosslight_flag_maintenance_cost
# memory / repo-size discussion: git kept rejecting pushes over GitHub's
# 2GB-per-pack limit once these were included in commit history.
# shaders/ is source code, not a binary asset, so it's the one exception.
assets/*
!assets/shaders/

# Exported builds -- same problem as assets/* above, just from `godot
# --export` instead of downloaded models. A macOS export bundle once landed
# in a commit here at 2.7GB (Crosslight.pck alone) and was never meant to
# be tracked -- builds are a local artifact, not project source.
CrossLight.app/
*.app/
*.pck
Crosslight.exe
crosslight_build/

# Per-branch editing workflow: main.tscn was split into sub-scenes
# (rooms/scn/*.scn). The .tscn text versions are the "in progress editing"
# copies -- Claude can text-edit them directly, but they're 5-6x bigger
# than the binary .scn versions and only the .scn ones are the ones
# main_scene's dependency chain actually points to. Local only.
rooms/tscn/
rooms/estate_exterior.tscn
